                <pb facs="0386" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">694.113Lumber/121: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Neville</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-26T17:00:00+09:00">November 26, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 26—9:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>110. Department’s instruction 587 [<hi rendition="#italic">588</hi>], August 1st,
                    I have had conference with the Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs. He informs me
                    that the committee has not yet reached a discussion of the lumber tariff and
                    asked me for a formal note setting forth the American position. I shall prepare
                    and send such note using Department’s instruction as a basis and refer to my
                    conversation with Minister for Foreign Affairs of August 30th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neville</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
